{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676082",
      "title": "Working with Nested Headers",
      "lectureOrder": 107,
      "videoOrder": 100,
      "sourceHash": "a3b37445c67caa82de551f18bc5805ad1dbcaac4aa5744c46f4fc17e9e576145",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.69,
          "en": "Now just like the meta function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.69,
          "end": 6.81,
          "en": "the headers function also is quite powerful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.81,
          "end": 9.63,
          "en": "For example, here I got a couple of marketing pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.63,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "which all don't really change too often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 15.09,
          "en": "They have no dynamic content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.09,
          "end": 18.9,
          "en": "Sure, I have a off form where users can switch to off mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.9,
          "end": 21.33,
          "en": "but I'm talking about the content of the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.33,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "We have that switch between login and sign up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "but the respective content is pretty static.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 28.41,
          "en": "It doesn't change all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.41,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "We don't add new off modes dynamically for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "So for off index and pricing we have pretty static data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 37.233,
          "en": "which doesn't change too often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "Now we can therefore use the same header setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 44.763,
          "en": "in all three pages and copy this into all three pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "However, this means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 48.66,
          "en": "that whenever we want to change this duration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.66,
          "end": 51.273,
          "en": "we have to do that in all three pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 53.94,
          "en": "Now this is rather cumbersome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "and we might have more marketing pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "and it would then get even more cumbersome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "and therefore we can instead go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "to the parent route of these three marketing routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 67.44,
          "en": "which is a pathless route, but this does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.44,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "We can add headers there as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.14,
          "end": 71.82300000000001,
          "en": "and export some headers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "Now, if you do that, you could think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 78.33,
          "en": "that distant automatically applies these headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78.33,
          "end": 81.42,
          "en": "to all child routes, but this won't happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.42,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "Here for example, pricing doesn't have its own headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 87.96000000000001,
          "en": "and as a result you will see that if I save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.96000000000001,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "and I go to pricing and I reload here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "we have no cash control headers here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 96.06,
          "en": "on the response headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.06,
          "end": 98.82,
          "en": "So the parent route headers are not applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.82,
          "end": 102.3,
          "en": "Remix does not automatically apply parent route headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.3,
          "end": 105.6,
          "en": "because this would also make it quite easy to mess things up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.6,
          "end": 109.14,
          "en": "by accidentally, for example caching things much longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.14,
          "end": 110.463,
          "en": "than you intended to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 115.65,
          "en": "But what you can do with your headers set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.65,
          "end": 118.86,
          "en": "in a parent route is the following.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.86,
          "end": 121.29,
          "en": "You can add your headers in a child route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.29,
          "end": 125.28,
          "en": "and then just like meta headers, except some extra data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.28,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "which is passed and automatically by Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 132,
          "en": "To be precise, headers gets an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "with an action headers, a loader headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "and a parent headers property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 142.44,
          "en": "Now these are then themselves headers objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.44,
          "end": 144.57,
          "en": "which give you access to the headers returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.57,
          "end": 149.57,
          "en": "by your action, your loader, or by your parent routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.7,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "So for example, here in pricing, we have headers returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "by our parent route, and then we can use the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "parent headers here to call the get method on this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 164.76,
          "en": "which is a method that exists on this header's object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.76,
          "end": 168.333,
          "en": "to get the cache control header from the parent route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.62,
          "end": 172.47,
          "en": "With that, we're setting this cash control header here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 174.96,
          "en": "in the parent route and in all child routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.96,
          "end": 176.403,
          "en": "we can access it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "And even though we still have to add the headers function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 183.03,
          "en": "for this, we now have one central place where we define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.03,
          "end": 186.12,
          "en": "the setting for this header and in all other places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "we then just access this central setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 190.74,
          "en": "And therefore we can copy this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.74,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "into all these marketing routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 195.213,
          "en": "to easily set the same headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.65,
          "end": 199.82999999999998,
          "en": "If we now save all files and I reload the pricing page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.82999999999998,
          "end": 203.43,
          "en": "you see that now there we do have this cash control header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.43,
          "end": 206.25,
          "en": "which is actually controlled by the parent route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 209.463,
          "en": "At least the value is controlled by the parent route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.69,
          "end": 212.73,
          "en": "So that's also something you can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.73,
          "end": 216.423,
          "en": "to attach your own headers to your page responses.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
